This project is licensed in four parts, because it contains four kinds of
thing.  Read the part that covers the file you are interested in.

  1. The game — engine, editor, code, writing, design.  © 2026 Grant van Zyl,
     licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.  Everything except the files listed in parts 2,
     3 and 4.

  2. The character sprite art and the world atlas.  Third-party pixel art by
     the Liberated Pixel Cup community, licensed OGA-BY 3.0 (some contributions
     CC0).  NOT covered by part 1 — see below.

  3. The CC-BY-SA 3.0 sheets: art/sprites/sanitary.png, art/sprites/wood.png,
     art/sprites/frontage.png and art/sprites/roofs.png.  Third-party pixel art
     by Matthew Nash and by bluecarrot16 and others.  ShareAlike, so it carries an obligation parts
     1 and 2 do not, and each work is kept in a file of its own for exactly
     that reason — see below.

  4. The CC-BY-SA 4.0 sheets: art/sprites/victorian.png and
     art/sprites/cars.png.  Third-party pixel art — the first compiled by
     bluecarrot16 from many LPC contributors, the second by tokka — licensed
     CC-BY-SA 4.0.  ShareAlike again, but a different version of it, which is
     why they are not part 3 — see below.  Two separate works on the same
     terms, in two separate files.

The split is deliberate.  Part 1's NoDerivatives term is ours to place on our
own work; it is not ours to place on somebody else's art, and doing so would
misrepresent the terms that art actually carries.  Parts 2, 3 and 4 are
separate from each other for the mirror-image reason: a ShareAlike term is not
ours to place on another artist's work, and packing two sets into one sheet
would do precisely that.

Parts 3 and 4 are separate from EACH OTHER because CC-BY-SA 3.0 and CC-BY-SA
4.0 are not the same licence.  They differ in ways that reach exactly what a
licence section has to get right — how an Adaptation may be relicensed, and
how attribution and notice must be given — so one section covering both would
be wrong about one of them.  Neither is "the ShareAlike part"; each is its own.


